  "body": "Improve CamCraft's MCP import and model-link tools (`crates/app/src/mcp/`) so an AI chat turn can hand off a part from SolidCraft and inspect what changed on re-import.\n\n## Scope\n- Update the `import_model` tool description in `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs` to list `.sc` and `.solidcraft` alongside STL, STEP, and OBJ.\n- Return the recorded `ModelSource` link (`path`, `sha256`) from `import_model` (`crates/app/src/script/api.rs`) when importing from disk.\n- When `import_model` updates an existing model through `UpdateModel`, return the structured `revision::FeatureChanges` summary (counts of carried, added, and missing faces, patches, and chains) so the chat knows which operations went `stale` and why.\n- Add `set_model_link` to `CORE_TOOLS` in `crates/app/src/mcp/provider.rs` so local models can inspect or unlink live CAD links.\n- Keep `import_model` behind `GateKind::FilePathAccess` (`crates/app/src/mcp/live.rs`) and never regenerate or post automatically on model updates.\n\nDone means: Headless MCP tests verify `import_model` on a `.sc` fixture returns `source` metadata, updating that model returns structured `changes` counts and marks dependent operations `stale` without regenerating or posting, and `tools_in(Provider::OpenAiChat, ToolSet::Core)` includes `set_model_link`.\n\nPart of #3793\n",
